From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: agent <agent@local>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 10:38:48 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] SourbyCraft - reject a landed arrow before the projectile tag
 lookup

AbstractArrow.isPickable evaluated super.isPickable() first, which is a
tag-set membership lookup for REDIRECTABLE_PROJECTILE, and only then the
boolean field read isInGround(). Both operands are pure reads, so the
order is free, and an arrow that has landed -- what an arrow spends most
of its life being -- can reject without touching the tag set at all.

Measured rather than guessed: a live overload on a real server put 806 of
832 samples in the hottest stack under canHitEntity ->
canBeHitByProjectile -> Holder.is -> ReferenceOpenHashSet.contains, and
this call is how that stack is reached. Projectile collision asks every
nearby candidate whether it is pickable, so the cost scales with local
projectile density -- the exact case that stalled the region.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/entity/projectile/arrow/AbstractArrow.java b/net/minecraft/world/entity/projectile/arrow/AbstractArrow.java
index 449d211ed59b27f1878c472e974ca8573b546d84..28656a78364ae948d48bdfa897eb2123bf73f549 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/entity/projectile/arrow/AbstractArrow.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/entity/projectile/arrow/AbstractArrow.java
@@ -813,7 +813,13 @@ public abstract class AbstractArrow extends Projectile {
 
     @Override
     public boolean isPickable() {
-        return super.isPickable() && !this.isInGround();
+        // SourbyCraft - cheap test first. super.isPickable() is a tag-set membership lookup
+        // (REDIRECTABLE_PROJECTILE); isInGround() reads a boolean field. Both are pure, so the
+        // order is free to choose, and a landed arrow -- which is what an arrow spends most of
+        // its life being -- now rejects without touching the tag set. Measured: a live overload
+        // put 806 of 832 samples in the hottest stack under canHitEntity -> canBeHitByProjectile
+        // -> Holder.is -> ReferenceOpenHashSet.contains, reached through exactly this call.
+        return !this.isInGround() && super.isPickable();
     }
 
     @Override
